  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Finely chop the onion and capsicum. Thinly slice the jalapeno. Crush or finely chop 2 garlic cloves. Combine 1 tbs white vinegar and 1 tsp sugar in a bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the onion and capsicum and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352284/photos/large/116845_1-0ab95d066d6e3ef53c643cde508d925c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook plant-based mince: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Cook the plant-based mince, breaking up the lumps with a spoon, for 5-6 mins until browned. Add the garlic, Tex-Mex seasoning and 2 tbs water and cook, stirring, for 3 mins or until slightly thickened. Remove from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352285/photos/large/116845_2-89bf93b5823ff16ce95708af653523d9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make cowboy candy: Meanwhile, put 1 tbs white vinegar and 3 tsp sugar in a small saucepan and stir to combine. Cook over medium-high heat, stirring, for 4-5 mins until golden and the sugar is dissolved. Stir in the jalapeno (see Kitchen 101), then remove from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352286/photos/large/116845_3-d370a666463cef0cb68f764cee8db010.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tortillas: Put the tortillas on a plate, slightly overlapping, and microwave for 30 secs or until warmed through (see Cooking tip).",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352287/photos/large/116845_4-fae920cfbe5dfb17c3de947440cf6f03.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Spread the tortillas with the mayonnaise and top with the plant-based mince, salsa and cowboy candy. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352288/photos/large/116845_5-119fdfca7948e14b5e1735daff0cc62e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Cowboy candy is another name for candied jalapeno. The chilli has a mild heat, so if someone in your household prefers no spice, serve the cowboy candy at the table instead.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1352289/photos/large/116845_6-9d0cb3d29f7cad58db7e260ee0a9fb35.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
